 "overview": "This file (894.20290/1) comprises a February 1944 diplomatic despatch from the U.S. Embassy in Buenos Aires to the Secretary of State transmitting an extensive 23-page reference directory of Japanese wartime organizations, together with a subsequent State Department memorandum circulating the intelligence to U.S. military and security agencies. Sourced from the April 29, 1943 issue of the English-language Nippon Times Weekly loaned by a former Argentine consul in Yokohama, the directory catalogs over one hundred major Japanese newspapers, chambers of commerce, and semi-official bodies handling economic, cultural, religious, educational, scientific, propaganda, tourist, and colonial endeavors across the Greater East Asia Sphere. Each entry records the organization's address, leadership—prominently featuring aristocrats, cabinet ministers, military generals, and industrial leaders such as Prince Fumimaro Konoye, General Kuniaki Koiso, and Aiichiro Fujiyama—as well as institutional objectives, overseas branches, and active publications. Upon receipt in Washington in March 1944, the State Department transmitted copies directly to the Military Intelligence Division, the Office of Naval Intelligence, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, and the Office of Strategic Services, reflecting the critical value of open-source Japanese institutional data for Allied wartime operations.",
