    "Domei Tsushin Sha"
   ],
   "start_page": 2,
   "summary": "This 23-page enclosure contains an extensive roster of Japanese organizations across fourteen categories: influential newspapers, chambers of commerce, religion, propaganda, diplomatic and bilateral associations, colonization, tourism, literature and arts, trade, medical and racial science, industry, education, economic and cultural research, and miscellaneous public associations. Each entry provides the organizational headquarters address, leadership, stated mission, overseas activities or branches, and official publications. The directory details the coordination of Japanese political elites, aristocrats, industrialists, and military figures in directing wartime economic exploitation, ideological indoctrination, and cultural penetration across occupied Asia and the Pacific.",
   "title": "Enclosure: List of Organizations in Japan Handling Economic, Cultural, Religious, Propaganda, Educational, Press, Colonization, Tourist, and Other Endeavors in the Greater East Asia Sphere",
   "to": "U.S. Embassy, Buenos Aires / Department of State"
  },
